{"t": 1794113424.8127272, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "Pipeline fix for the red `main` pipeline (#8812, failed job `test:contract` #77104).\n\n**Root cause:** `billing/invoice.py` formatted the sequence with plain `{seq}`, so `invoice_number(2026, 42)` returned `INV-2026-42`. The ERP import contract (FIN-77) requires the sequence part to be zero-padded to 6 digits, so the contract test failed with `'INV-2026-42' != 'INV-2026-000042'`.\n\n**Fix:** format the sequence as `{seq:06d}` in `billing/invoice.py`, which yields `INV-2026-000042`.\n\n**Verification:** the exact contract assertion `invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"` now passes locally, as do the boundary checks `seq=0` -> `INV-2026-000000` and a 6-digit sequence (`999999`), which is unchanged. The change only affects sequences shorter than 6 digits.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
